The feedback store's directory — committed EMPTY, on purpose.

deploy/docker-compose.yml binds this directory into the orchestrator READ-WRITE
(../../feedback:/data/feedback) while the rest of the repository stays read-only.
A bind mount whose source does not exist is CREATED BY DOCKER, owned by root, and
the orchestrator runs as uid 10002 — so without this file a fresh clone gets a
directory the store cannot write to, and the only symptom is a warning per marker.

What lands here (gepa-feedback.jsonl) is gitignored: it holds full model prompts,
full model replies and source excerpts from the repositories under analysis.

See orchestrator/README.md, "The feedback store".
